---
arrangement: why-improvement-ran-blind
when-used: The IMPROVEMENTS item for a site that ran with no read-only check behind it -- the aggregate row that turns an un-oracled command into a next step.
why: 28L rul-full-driver-this-arc: the zero-argument `dorc why` aggregate is driven in-process here, so every row it reaches has an editable home rather than a lock-only one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# Two un-oracled commands and nothing described: the whole run is unprobed, which is exactly the
# world the IMPROVEMENTS panel exists to report. `hork` is the corpus's inert stand-in mutator.
hork tune --profile web
apt-get install -y nginx

